      "id": "M4154-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "A. A colleague calls every normalized weighted feature sum \"Dempster evidence fusion\" and calls belief masses calibrated class probabilities. For the frame Θ={A,B}, take m1(A)=0.6,m1(B)=0.1,m1(Θ)=0.3; m2(A)=0.2,m2(B)=0.5,m2(Θ)=0.3. Calculate the standard normalized conjunctive/Dempster combination and its conflict K, compare it with the arithmetic mean of masses, and calculate the pignistic class probabilities by distributing Θ equally. State the boundary for m1(A)=1,m2(B)=1. Does learning two heads on the same observations prove independent evidence sources? Write a positive English method sentence of at most45words for a different operation that really is just a softmax-weighted sum of feature vectors. Consult the current bank's complete-name admission/Chinese status: exactly what source pair and wording is actually recorded for Dempster's rule? If no completed record exists, say so; do not invent one, treat a preprint as a second work, or infer that an unlisted term is invalid. Is the full name \"Calibrated Causal Dempster Reliability Block\" admitted by a base rule?\n",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Preserve the conflict-normalized mass calculation, the different arithmetic mean, explicit probability conversion and total-conflict boundary.",
        "Report the actually recorded source pair/Chinese scope and distinguish learned heads, calibrated reliability and complete proposed names."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Call normalized feature sums Dempster combination, conflate belief masses with calibrated probabilities or silently repair K=1 with epsilon.",
        "Invent source independence or a completed complete-name/Chinese admission record from an adjacent base entry."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Preserves conflict-normalized masses, the different arithmetic mean, explicit probability conversion and K=1 boundary; reports the scoped P49/P84 theoretical pair and separate Chinese variants without assuming source independence or full-name admission.",
