    {
      "id": "M4154-B",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "B. Draft an English abstract115–140words and one contribution≤40words from only this fictional method contract. Preserve the approved proposed English name MassLink; no approved Chinese full name exists and novelty comparison remains pending. Task: fault classification from two aligned sensor streams of an industrial process with known class set, not open-set detection. Each encoder/head outputs nonnegative class evidence; α=e+1 defines its Dirichlet model; singleton belief masses b=e/S and residual mass u=C/S form an opinion, C is known-class count and S=sum α. A learned coefficient from the corresponding stream's encoded features discounts singleton masses and transfers remaining mass to Θ. It is a learned weight, not demonstrated accuracy calibration. The two discounted mass functions are combined using the standard normalized Dempster rule, for K<1. Total conflict returns a declared abstention, not epsilon denominator repair. Pignistic probabilities are used for the final class decision. Two held-out industrial-process cases show improved balanced accuracy relative to the same two separately evaluated heads. No latency, deployment, cross-plant, calibrated probability, causal, independent-source or unknown-class claim has been tested. Connect acquisition/object challenge -> evidence representation -> weighting -> actual combination -> decision -> observed comparison. Do not turn the abstract into a list of equations or routine settings; no invented module graph, numerical performance, novelty proof or defensive 'not X' prose. Separate any author-only verification notes. State exact word counts.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Preserve aligned streams, Dirichlet-derived masses, learned source discounting, actual mass combination, declared abstention and final classification.",
        "Keep the approved fictional English name, pending novelty and matched two-case balanced-accuracy comparison without defensive prose."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent open-set, causal, cross-plant, runtime, deployment or calibrated-probability evidence.",
